# Secrets — never commit
.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Data — raw and interim are reproducible from MANIFEST, never versioned
data/raw/**
data/interim/**
data/processed/**
!data/**/.gitkeep
!data/**/*.md
# The seven benchmark-station rows of the OpenAQ location census, metadata only (id,
# city, provider, is_monitor, licence). These facts are already published in MANIFEST's
# per-instrument table; committing them lets extract_numbers.py derive instrument grade
# from a clean clone instead of failing on the gitignored full census.
!data/station_census_benchmark.csv

# BUT: the frozen benchmark splits ARE the deliverable and MUST be committed.
!benchmark/splits/**

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Experiment logs — the SQLite DB is a local cache; the CSV export is committed

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Private brief and internal audit trail — kept locally, not published.
# `message.txt` is the author's own working brief; `review/` holds adversarial reviewer
# reports and large before/after snapshots produced during the QC repair. Both were useful
# internally and neither belongs in a public release attached to a submission: the reviewer
# reports argue positions the authors do not hold, and reading them out of context would
# misrepresent the work. The scientific record they produced is public in the places it
# belongs -- data/DECISIONS.md (decisions D-001..D-012) and the manuscript itself.
message.txt
message*.txt
prompt.txt
prompt*.txt
review/

# Also internal, for the same reason. `JOURNAL_STRATEGY.md` records venue selection together
# with the team's financial position and APC-waiver case -- personal information that has no
# place in a public repository attached to a submission. `next.md` is an engineering handoff
# that references the quarantined audit trail above.
JOURNAL_STRATEGY.md
next.md

# Internal project-management documents. Superseded or venue-specific, and misleading to a
# reader of the public repository: SUBMISSION.md still described an arXiv -> Environmental
# Modelling & Software route, and STATUS.md / PLAN.md / PAPER_CLAIM.md still described the
# project as being at "Phase 0". ECO_PULSY_INTEGRATION.md documents a separate application.
# All remain on disk; the current state is in the manuscripts and data/DECISIONS.md.
SUBMISSION.md
STATUS.md
PLAN.md
PAPER_CLAIM.md
ECO_PULSY_INTEGRATION.md

# Internal release/integrity audit working documents. Same reason as review/: these record
# process (author consent chasing, admissions framing, defect triage), not science.
audit/

# Generated release artefacts. The Zenodo ZIP is built from a commit, never committed to it.
dist/
